SPBilly_UniqueSkill_06_Desc:
Starlight Billy gains extra Sheer Force based on his Max HP, with every 1 point of Max HP increasing Sheer Force by 0.1;
All <color=#F0D12B>Physical Attribute DMG</color> dealt by Starlight Billy's skills is Sheer DMG, ignoring enemy DEF and using his Sheer Force stat as the skill DMG Multiplier; Starlight Billy recovers {EXCEL:9} Adrenaline when entering the battlefield. This effect can trigger once every 60 seconds in Investigation Zones;
When Starlight Billy takes fatal damage, he negates that damage and gains a Shield equal to 180% of his Max HP, lasting {EXCEL:10} seconds. This effect can trigger once every 25 seconds. Damage taken in a single instance cannot exceed the Shield value;
While in <color=#FFFFFF>[Bike Mode]</color>, Starlight Billy continuously consumes HP, CRIT DMG is increased by 83%, DMG taken is reduced by 30%, and Anti-Interrupt Level is increased;
When Starlight Billy's HP drops below 1% of his Max HP while in <color=#FFFFFF>[Bike Mode]</color>, he enters <color=#FFFFFF>[Free Mode]</color>;
While in <color=#FFFFFF>[Bike Mode]</color>, dealing DMG with skills recovers <color=#FFFFFF>[Heat]</color>. The max <color=#FFFFFF>[Heat]</color> cap is 100. When <color=#FFFFFF>[Heat]</color> is full, the next <color=#FFFFFF>[EX Special Attack]</color> upgrades to <color=#FFFFFF>[EX Special Attack: Starlight Knight Flying Kick]</color>. Activating <color=#FFFFFF>[EX Special Attack: Starlight Knight Flying Kick]</color> consumes all <color=#FFFFFF>[Heat]</color>;
While in <color=#FFFFFF>[Free Mode]</color>, certain skills restore Starlight Billy's HP when they deal DMG. When Starlight Billy's current HP is at least 10%, he can activate <color=#FFFFFF>[Special Attack: All Aboard]</color> to enter <color=#FFFFFF>[Bike Mode]</color>.
Activating <color=#FFFFFF>[EX Special Attack: Moto Slam]</color> or activating <color=#FFFFFF>[Special Attack: Switch to Freestyle]</color> or <color=#FFFFFF>[Special Attack: Switch to Bike Mode]</color> and triggering a <color=#FFFFFF>[Perfect Dodge]</color> restores his HP;
Activating <color=#FFFFFF>[Basic Attack: Moto Dash]</color>, <color=#FFFFFF>[Basic Attack: Tail Whip]</color>, or <color=#FFFFFF>[Dodge Counter: Moto Drift]</color> grants a Shield equal to 3% of his Max HP. Shields can stack up to 50 times and last {EXCEL:8} seconds; repeated triggers reset the duration;

Astra_Talent_04_Desc_01_Realign:
After activating a <color=#FFFFFF>Chain Attack</color> or <color=#FFFFFF>Ultimate</color>, within 15s, Astra Yao can trigger a <color=#FFFFFF>Quick Assist</color> even if she does not have <color=#FFFFFF>Chords</color>. When the attack hits an enemy, the interval for triggering a <color=#FFFFFF>Quick Assist</color> is reduced to 1s.
While in the <color=#FFFFFF>Idyllic Cadenza</color> state, when other squad members enter the field via a <color=#FFFFFF>Quick Assist</color>, they will receive different buffs based on their specialty, and this effect can be triggered once every 3s for the entire squad:
<color=#FFFFFF>Attack</color>: The next <color=#FFFFFF>Quick Assist</color> heavy attack on an enemy will deal extra DMG equal to 300% of Astra Yao's ATK;
<color=#FFFFFF>Anomaly</color>: The next <color=#FFFFFF>Quick Assist</color> will have 50% increased Anomaly Buildup;
<color=#FFFFFF>Stun</color>: The next <color=#FFFFFF>Quick Assist</color> will inflict 50% increased Daze.

